    "12-8":  "What is letting go in love is finishing — the long inner shift is approaching its end, the slow remaking is nearly complete. Let yourself stop bracing for the next hard turn. The work has nearly done its work on you.",
    "12-9":  "What is letting go in love is touching meaning — old convictions easing, the philosophy quietening, certainty becoming more spacious. Belief held with less grip is sometimes truer. Rest in the easing.",
    "12-10": "What is letting go in love is publicly visible — old commitments ending, visibility cooling. Use the lower attention well; do not chase what was leaving anyway. Some of your most honest love needs the camera off.",
    "12-11": "What is letting go in love is touching the wider circle — old friendships completing, network shapes you are outgrowing. Let the contact taper. The right people stay through change; the rest were never the load-bearing wall.",
    "12-12": "What is letting go in love runs on its own quiet rhythm right now. Endings, release, the dissolution of old shapes of bond — these are self-completing. There is a kind of grace in the easing. Do not interrupt it. Some completions are best held in silence.",
