    "Mars-6":  "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in the daily-tending. Heat shows up as the energy to keep going through small obstacles, fix what is broken in routine, push through the resistance of being close. Channel into one clean fix today rather than scattered complaints.",
    "Mars-7":  "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in close bonds. The bond keeps pulling toward direct conversation with the partner — the real disagreement, the honest air-clearing. Have the talk; avoidance costs more than the discomfort of directness.",
    "Mars-8":  "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in shared depths. Heat here is for long battles — power dynamics, deep changes that take real persistence. Choose your fights with leverage in mind; the wars worth winning here are strategic ones.",
    "Mars-9":  "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in meaning. The bond keeps connecting heat to conviction — the strong opinion about love, the principle you will not give up. Stand your ground without making it a war; conviction held cleanly does not need to bully.",
    "Mars-10": "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in the public face of the bond. Heat in visibility looks like decisive public action — taking the stand, claiming the commitment, moving on the offer. Walk into the room you have been hesitating outside of.",
    "Mars-11": "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in the wider circle. Heat here is for protecting the network — defending a friend, drawing a clean boundary in community, refusing to let a connection erode. Be direct without burning the bridge.",
    "Mars-12": "The part of you ready to fight is anchored in release. Some of the heat here is for endings — the courage to close the chapter, the energy to let go cleanly, the strength to walk away from what has run its course. Use it; endings sometimes require force, kindly applied.",

