    "Rahu-9":  "The part of you that hungers is anchored in meaning. The pull is toward foreign philosophies of love, new teachers, doctrines that promise to convert your path. Stay sober; big visions are real, they are also seductive. Walk toward the bigger picture but keep your feet on small steady steps.",
    "Rahu-10": "The part of you that hungers is anchored in the public face of the bond. The pull is toward more visible commitment — the next step, recognition, public claim. Walk toward it without pretending you do not want it; just keep the work that supports the bond growing alongside.",
    "Rahu-11": "The part of you that hungers is anchored in the wider circle. The pull is toward unfamiliar friends, foreign networks, opportunities arriving from places you did not plant. Receive the strange ones with curiosity; the new circle is the next chapter's seedbed.",
    "Rahu-12": "The part of you that hungers is anchored in release. The pull is toward leaving — quiet dreams of departure from love, foreign-feeling escapes, the wanting to dissolve the current shape. Sit with it; strong inner pulls deserve real listening before action.",

